@startuml animate-stick-figure-use-cases
title animate_stick_figure.py — Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Developer / Artist" as User
actor "Web Browser" as Browser

rectangle "JSONL → Stick-Figure HTML Tool" {
  usecase "Choose timestamped\nPose JSONL" as UC1
  usecase "Validate input and\noutput paths" as UC2
  usecase "Parse and normalize\nlandmarks" as UC3
  usecase "Sort frames by\ntimestamp" as UC4
  usecase "Generate standalone\nHTML file" as UC5
  usecase "Open animation page" as UC6
  usecase "Play / Pause" as UC7
  usecase "Restart animation" as UC8
  usecase "Seek to frame" as UC9
  usecase "Change playback speed" as UC10
  usecase "Draw stick figure and\nshow timestamp" as UC11
}

User --> UC1
User --> UC5
User --> UC6
UC5 .> UC2 : <<include>>
UC5 .> UC3 : <<include>>
UC5 .> UC4 : <<include>>
Browser --> UC6
Browser --> UC7
Browser --> UC8
Browser --> UC9
Browser --> UC10
UC7 .> UC11 : <<include>>
UC8 .> UC11 : <<include>>
UC9 .> UC11 : <<include>>
UC10 .> UC11 : <<include>>

note bottom of UC5
The script consumes existing Pose JSONL.
It does not extract landmarks from source video.
end note
note bottom of UC11
Playback is local and standalone;
no network service is required.
end note
@enduml
